.TH DDNSD 8 "November 2026" "ddnsd 0.0.9" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ddnsd \- dynamic DNS daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddnsd
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.br
.B ddnsd dry\-run
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.br
.B ddnsd pkarr\-keygen
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ddnsd
periodically finds this host's public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and keeps the
A and AAAA records of one or more domains pointed at them, using the
Cloudflare and No-IP DNS providers, or PKARR records on the Mainline DHT.
.PP
By default, each global address of the local network interfaces, or of one
interface, is published if an HTTP echo service (icanhazip, ifconfig.me,
ipify or custom URLs), asked from that address, sees it as itself; behind NAT,
the address the echo service sees can be published instead.
The addresses are looked up every
.B resolve_interval
seconds, and also at the next check after the global addresses of a local
interface change, e.g. after a WAN reconnect.
.PP
When a provider rejects an update in a way that needs the configuration to be
fixed, such as invalid credentials, the daemon stops updating that provider
until it is restarted after fixing the configuration. After server errors or
rate limiting it waits as long as the provider asks; other failed updates are
retried at the next check, every
.B tick
seconds.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dry\-run
Run one update pass without changing any records: the planned changes are
logged, and the providers are only read from. Exits with a non-zero status if
any provider failed.
.TP
.B pkarr\-keygen
Generate a random PKARR secret key. The secret, 64 hex digits for
.B secret_key
or
.BR secret_file ,
is printed to standard output, and its public key to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIconfig\fR
Read the configuration from
.IR config .
The default is
.IR /etc/ddnsd.toml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ddnsd.toml
The TOML configuration file. It contains provider credentials and must not be
readable by group or others, e.g. mode 0600.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.toml
An example configuration describing all settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/configuration.md.gz
The reference of all configuration settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.B debug
or
.BR ddnsd=debug ;
the default is
.BR info .
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and start the service:
.PP
.nf
.RS
install \-m 600 /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.toml /etc/ddnsd.toml
editor /etc/ddnsd.toml
systemctl start ddnsd
.RE
.fi
